    thinking: "**Initiating Plan Development**\n\nI\'m now in the interactive clarification phase, focusing on high-value questions to fully grasp the nuances. My goal is to extract the essential information without jumping into implementation details too early. I\'m keen on establishing a solid foundation before committing to any code changes.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Directions**\n\nI\'m now contemplating visual directions for the dashboard, considering the user\'s desire for a minimalist, non-AI-generated UI. I\'m leaning toward a Nordic Civic Instrument aesthetic, envisioning a warm stone and ink palette with a calm, utilitarian feel. Alternatively, I\'m exploring a Botanical Studio style with natural tones. I\'m also considering an Atmospheric Slate or Swiss Meteorological Almanac approach. Also, I need to integrate with the weather data source.\n\n\n**Clarifying Regional Focus**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the weather data source, and my thoughts lean toward Open-Meteo API due to its comprehensive, keyless access. I need to confirm the primary target region to ensure the data is relevant, considering options like Northern India, Global with auto-detect, or East Asia. I also need to confirm the primary target region / default city to be able to proceed.\n\n**Personalization Scope Defined**\n\nI\'m now outlining the personalization scope, and I\'ve honed in on three core directions. I\'m focusing on a household profile and interactive impact simulator with personalized routines, indoor air tips, and impact quantification. Also, I need to focus on family health and a daily planner that focuses on hourly outdoor safety, mask alerts, and kid/elderly schedules. I\'m also including community action and a neighborhood hub.\n\n\n"
