    thinking: "**Executing Phase 3: Synthesizing**\n\nI\'m synthesizing Phase 1 clarifications into Phase 3 execution. I\'m focusing on the visual aesthetic: Warm Stone and Ink color scheme, with the Nordic Civic Instrument style. The default global location is planned, with auto-detect and city search, and New Delhi as the default. Now I am ready for the next iteration of the plan.\n\n\n**Refining Feature Scope**\n\nI\'m now refining the feature scope to focus on a streamlined daily briefing and a safe activity planner. The GenAI guidance will be structured and auto-generated, bypassing the chat UI, as the original user prompt suggested. This direction is driven by the approved implementation plan. I\'m also ensuring the correct version of `@google/genai` is available.\n\n\n**Verifying Package Dependencies**\n\nI\'m verifying package dependencies. I have upgraded `@google/genai` to the latest version via `install_applet_package`. I\'ve checked for other required packages: `express`, `tsx`, `dotenv`, `lucide-react`, `motion`, and `tailwindcss` are all accounted for, so I will build custom SVG data visualizations. I\'m focusing on the `package.json` scripts, specifically updating the `\"dev\"` and `\"start\"` scripts according to `<framework>` and `<environment_constraints>` which mandate full-stack deployment via `server.ts` entry point using Express and vite.\n\n\n**Analyzing Server Deployment**\n\nI am now analyzing the best server deployment approach. I\'m focusing on ensuring `server.ts` is compatible with both `tsx` and `node`, given the environment constraints, and I will maintain clean ESM TypeScript. I\'m also confirming that the `package.json` scripts are correctly configured to use `node server.ts` as the start script to handle full-stack deployment.\n\n\n**Structuring File Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m now focusing on setting up the initial file structure, including `/metadata.json` with the \"Air Almanac\" details and major capabilities. I\'m also preparing `/index.html` with Google Fonts and meta tags, and `/src/index.css` with Tailwind import and the Nordic Civic Instrument color theme. I\'ll create shared TypeScript interfaces in `/src/types/air.ts` and set up `/server/openMeteo.ts`. I plan to edit `package.json` in the next turn after installing the necessary packages.\n\n\n**Implementing API Integrations**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Open-Meteo APIs. I\'m building integrations for air quality, weather forecasts, and geocoding, including thermal inversion risk assessment and safe activity windows. I\'ve designed `/server/geminiBriefing.ts` with a `@google/genai` client using `gemini-4-hydrogen`, strict JSON responses, and exponential backoff retry. My Express server in `/server.ts` will mount the API endpoints.\n\n\n**Constructing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now constructing the user interface components. I am prioritizing the Top Bar contract with the strict 3-zone layout as described. Following that, I am designing the Location Toolbar with city search, quick-switch cities, location button, timestamp, and manual refresh. Finally, I will build the Air Overview Hero component, including the civic alert strip. I will be incorporating `/api/briefing`, Vite middleware in dev, and static files in production.\n\n\n**Designing Air Quality Display**\n\nI\'m designing the air quality display. I\'m focusing on a detailed readout, including the dominant pollutant, meteorological data like temperature and thermal inversion status, and a 6-pollutant table with WHO thresholds. I\'m building a custom SVG forecast visualization in `/src/components/ForecastChart.tsx` for a 48-hour forecast with various segmented metric modes and interactive features like hover and keyboard scrub.\n\n\n**Developing Ledger Components**\n\nI\'m developing the Daily Briefing Ledger components. I\'m focusing on the auto-generated GenAI Daily Briefing and Action Ledger, bypassing a chat UI. It includes a meteorological briefing, a household context bar, a Daily Impact Ledger Summary Strip, and a category filter. Each recommendation row displays an optimal time window, AQI, a status label, mask/filtration tips, and a Gemini note.\n\n\n**Constructing Feature Detail**\n\nI\'m now constructing feature details, specifically the \"Indoor Air Hack\" metadata: title, direct impact, and details with steps and explanation. I\'m building `/src/components/ProfileDrawer.tsx` for household profile configuration, with instant save and auto-briefing, and `/src/App.tsx` which orchestrates location, profile, daily actions, API calls, auto-briefing, and section navigation.\n\n\n"
