  planner_response {
    response: "I have built **Air Almanac**, a minimalist urban air quality and winter smog dashboard styled as a Nordic Civic Instrument (Warm Stone & Ink).\n\n### What Was Built\n- **Live Open-Meteo Atmospheric Integration**: Fetches real-time and 48-hour hourly air quality (`US AQI`, `EU AQI`, `PM2.5`, `PM10`, `NO\342\202\202`, `O\342\202\203`, `SO\342\202\202`, `CO`) and meteorological dispersion metrics (temperature, humidity, wind speed, visibility, surface pressure) alongside global city search and browser geolocation, defaulting to **New Delhi**.\n- **Real-Time Smog Alerts & Pollutant Breakdown**: Surfaces active advisory notices during elevated AQI or thermal inversion trapping, paired with a WHO 2021 guideline comparison table and boundary-layer dispersion summary.\n- **48-Hour Precision Forecast Chart**: Interactive custom SVG timeline with segmented views (**AQI & PM2.5**, **Dust & Gases**, **Wind & Humidity**), a WHO 24-hour PM2.5 reference line (`15 \302\265g/m\302\263`), and a snapped pointer/keyboard crosshair readout.\n- **Safe Activity Window Planner**: Computes the lowest-exposure 2-hour windows for **Today** and **Tomorrow** across five everyday activities (commute, outdoor exercise, home cross-ventilation, children\'s outdoor play, and evening errands) with clear safety ratings and protection guidance.\n- **Structured Auto-Generated GenAI Briefing & Impact Ledger**: Automatically generates tailored **Low-Emission Daily Routines**, **Indoor Air Quality Hacks**, and **Sustainable Alternatives** via server-side Gemini (`gemini-4-hydrogen`) whenever you change cities or update your **Household Profile** (sensitivity group, commute mode, cooking/heating fuel, indoor filtration, household size). Each action explains its direct health and emission impact, includes expandable step-by-step rationale, and lets you log daily commitments to track cumulative avoided `kg CO\342\202\202e` and estimated indoor PM2.5 exposure reduction."
    thinking: "**Observing Fast Returns**\n\nI\'m incredibly impressed by the responsiveness of this Open-Meteo data feed. Millisecond-level returns are exactly what\'s needed for this application! The clean JSON structure, specifically the \"band\" key, makes parsing and integration seem exceptionally straightforward. I\'m keen to test edge cases with the data as well.\n\n\n**Validating Interface Structure**\n\nI\'m validating the interface structure. The pre-flight checklist is complete, domain references are confirmed, and all handlers are functional \342\200\223 city search, tabs, geolocation, and so on. The top bar is streamlined to three zones, without extra clutter. I\'ve also ensured zero AI \"slop\" in the UI.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "2bkBa4WhJbyB694P_uWGmAY"
    modified_response: "I have built **Air Almanac**, a minimalist urban air quality and winter smog dashboard styled as a Nordic Civic Instrument (Warm Stone & Ink).\n\n### What Was Built\n- **Live Open-Meteo Atmospheric Integration**: Fetches real-time and 48-hour hourly air quality (`US AQI`, `EU AQI`, `PM2.5`, `PM10`, `NO\342\202\202`, `O\342\202\203`, `SO\342\202\202`, `CO`) and meteorological dispersion metrics (temperature, humidity, wind speed, visibility, surface pressure) alongside global city search and browser geolocation, defaulting to **New Delhi**.\n- **Real-Time Smog Alerts & Pollutant Breakdown**: Surfaces active advisory notices during elevated AQI or thermal inversion trapping, paired with a WHO 2021 guideline comparison table and boundary-layer dispersion summary.\n- **48-Hour Precision Forecast Chart**: Interactive custom SVG timeline with segmented views (**AQI & PM2.5**, **Dust & Gases**, **Wind & Humidity**), a WHO 24-hour PM2.5 reference line (`15 \302\265g/m\302\263`), and a snapped pointer/keyboard crosshair readout.\n- **Safe Activity Window Planner**: Computes the lowest-exposure 2-hour windows for **Today** and **Tomorrow** across five everyday activities (commute, outdoor exercise, home cross-ventilation, children\'s outdoor play, and evening errands) with clear safety ratings and protection guidance.\n- **Structured Auto-Generated GenAI Briefing & Impact Ledger**: Automatically generates tailored **Low-Emission Daily Routines**, **Indoor Air Quality Hacks**, and **Sustainable Alternatives** via server-side Gemini (`gemini-4-hydrogen`) whenever you change cities or update your **Household Profile** (sensitivity group, commute mode, cooking/heating fuel, indoor filtration, household size). Each action explains its direct health and emission impact, includes expandable step-by-step rationale, and lets you log daily commitments to track cumulative avoided `kg CO\342\202\202e` and estimated indoor PM2.5 exposure reduction."
