  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering API Key Mystery**\n\nI\'ve just realized the `GEMINI_API_KEY` isn\'t accessible in the `run_command` shell environment. It appears the API key is injected directly into the dev server\'s process by AI Studio. This explains a lot! Also, it has jogged my memory about task-80 taking so long on the real dev server (that server DOES have the API key available).\n\n\n**Optimizing Model Configuration**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on optimizing the model configuration. I\'m leaning toward using `\'gemini-4-hydrogen\'` with `ThinkingLevel.LOW` for its balance of quality and speed. I\'m keen to compare its performance against `\'gemini-3.1-flash-lite\'` with `ThinkingLevel.MINIMAL` using the `gemini-api` SKILL.md. My goal is to fine-tune the prompt and schema to keep the total token count within a 600-800 token range.\n\n\n**Confirming Live Location Bug**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the Kolkata live location bug. The user report is clear: Kolkata data is showing New Delhi\'s. I\'m focusing on `src/App.tsx`, `src/components/LocationToolbar.tsx`, `server.ts`, and `server/openMeteo.ts`. Specifically, I\'m scrutinizing lines 173\342\200\223204 in `src/App.tsx` and tracing how live location data is handled. This is top priority now. The goal is pinpoint and fix this live location bug.\n\n\n**Analyzing Location Handling**\n\nI\'m now laser-focused on the location data flow. I\'ve spotted a critical issue in `src/App.tsx`. Specifically, when the page first loads, the `location` data is incorrect. It appears to be an uninitialized state. Then the live location gets the raw latitude/longitude in *decimal degrees* and assigns it to `loc.country`. This is then converted to a string when the data is passed to `server.ts`. I think this is where the bug manifests. I\'m going to make sure the longitude/latitude is ALWAYS in the proper format.\n\n\n**Tracing Location Update Flow**\n\nI\'m now carefully retracing the location update flow. I see that the app starts with `DEFAULT_CITY` (**New Delhi**). The slow initial `fetchBriefing` call for New Delhi is a problem. The user\'s \"Use my location\" click triggers `navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition`, leading to Kolkata coordinates (`22.57, 88.36`). I\'ve spotted two bugs. Bug 1: `snapshot` isn\'t cleared when `airLoading` is running. Bug 2:  `fetchAir` and `fetchBriefing` lack any abort controllers or request guards! The initial New Delhi call finishes long after Kolkata has loaded. This explains why Kolkata is showing New Delhi\'s briefing.\n\n\n**Fixing Location Handling**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a critical failure in geolocation handling. I\'ve uncovered a series of bugs: first, the app never reverse-geocodes `(latitude, longitude)` into the correct city name. Second, `maximumAge: 300000` is susceptible to serving stale browser locations, especially near New Delhi. Third, I discovered a subtle issue in `server/openMeteo.ts` on line 258. It looks like an empty string for the latitude/longitude could lead to a flawed cache key. I\'m going to implement some robust checks and reverse geocoding to address these problems.\n\n\n**Refining Location Fixes**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on more location handling problems. **BUG 5** appears to be in `ForecastChart.tsx`, with `activeIndex` not resetting on city changes due to React re-using the instance. I\'ll pass a unique key. **BUG 6** is in `src/App.tsx`, and I\'m going to clear `snapshot` and `briefing` on city change to eliminate data bleed. Finally, I\'m going to work on improving the user experience of the \'use my location\' feature.\n\n\n\n**Improving Location Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on improving the user experience of location display during \"Use my location.\" If the browser returns location data, I will show the precise reverse-geocoded city plus coordinates in the `LocationToolbar`. I also aim to enable an instant city switch if the browser\'s geolocation resolves to a different city. I\'ll add `enableHighAccuracy: true, maximumAge: 0, timeout: 10000` to prevent stale data. I am also adding Kolkata to `PRESET_CITIES`. Finally, I\'m rechecking `server/openMeteo.ts` to ensure data integrity.\n\n\n**Analyzing Cache Interactions**\n\nI\'m now carefully analyzing cache interactions. I see the cache key relies on `(lat.toFixed(2), lon.toFixed(2))`, which can lead to missed cache hits. I\'m focusing on `src/App.tsx`, specifically lines 69-70, to understand how `location` is set via `loadStoredLocation`. This variable persists between visits. I also noticed that the `useEffect` call for `fetchAir` is being triggered concurrently with `handleUseGeolocation`, and I must account for this behavior.\n\n\n**Implementing Reverse Geocoding**\n\nI\'m now implementing reverse geocoding to address a critical flaw. The app previously lacked this functionality, leading to inaccurate city displays.  I\'ve added a `reverseGeocode` function that calls OpenStreetMap Nominatim. I\'m extracting the `city`, `town`, `village`, `suburb`, `state_district`, or `county` information to get the correct location names. This should address the issue in the location flow.\n\n\n**Refining Gemini Configuration**\n\nI\'m now refining the Gemini configuration to optimize briefing generation. I\'m importing `ThinkingLevel` and setting `thinkingConfig` to `ThinkingLevel.LOW` on `gemini-4-hydrogen`, for fast response times. I\'m also adding an in-memory briefing cache with a 5-minute expiry, keyed by relevant parameters, and adding a 25-second timeout safety net to requests. I also need to make updates to reverse geocoding to retrieve `city`, and other data, with a coordinate fallback.\n\n\n**Enhancing Location Handling**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial features for enhanced location handling. I\'m adding a `/api/reverse-geocode?lat=...&lon=...` endpoint and calling `reverseGeocode(lat, lon)`. I\'m also tightening coordinate parsing in `GET /api/air-data` and passing a `forceRefresh` flag to `generateDailyBriefing`. Additionally, Kolkata is added to `PRESET_CITIES`. Finally, I\'m setting up `AbortController` refs and sequence IDs to prevent data from prior cities from being displayed. I\'m also clearing `snapshot` and `briefing` on new city selection.\n\n\n**Improving Geolocation Display**\n\nI\'m now focused on delivering an improved geolocation display for the user. I\'m upgrading `handleUseGeolocation` by using `{ enableHighAccuracy: true, timeout: 10000, maximumAge: 0 }` for precise location results. I\'m calling `/api/reverse-geocode` immediately for an accurate city display, such as \"Kolkata, West Bengal, India\". I\'m passing `forceRefresh = true` to guarantee fresh data. I am also updating chart keying and components to remove data bleed.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "Jr0Ba4WMONbv-8YP487iqA8"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1596474228854486659"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Add Nominatim reverseGeocode helper to server/openMeteo.ts so browser geolocation resolves to real city names like Kolkata, West Bengal, India\", \"EndLine\":254, \"Instruction\":\"Add reverseGeocode function right after searchCities in server/openMeteo.ts\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"  return (payload.results ?? []).map((item) => ({\\n    name: item.name,\\n    admin1: item.admin1,\\n    country: item.country ?? \'Unknown\',\\n    latitude: item.latitude,\\n    longitude: item.longitude,\\n    timezone: item.timezone,\\n  }));\\n}\\n\\nexport async function reverseGeocode(latitude: number, longitude: number): Promise<LocationInfo> {\\n  const fallback: LocationInfo = {\\n    name: \'Current Location\',\\n    country: `${Math.abs(latitude).toFixed(2)}\302\260${latitude >= 0 ? \'N\' : \'S\'}, ${Math.abs(longitude).toFixed(2)}\302\260${longitude >= 0 ? \'E\' : \'W\'}`,\\n    latitude,\\n    longitude,\\n  };\\n\\n  try {\\n    const controller = new AbortController();\\n    const timer = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 4500);\\n    const url = `https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/reverse?lat=${encodeURIComponent(\\n      String(latitude)\\n    )}&lon=${encodeURIComponent(String(longitude))}&format=jsonv2&zoom=10`;\\n\\n    const res = await fetch(url, {\\n      signal: controller.signal,\\n      headers: {\\n        \'User-Agent\': \'AirAlmanac/1.0 (civic-air-dashboard)\',\\n        \'Accept-Language\': \'en\',\\n      },\\n    });\\n    clearTimeout(timer);\\n\\n    if (!res.ok) {\\n      return fallback;\\n    }\\n\\n    const data = (await res.json()) as {\\n      name?: string;\\n      address?: {\\n        city?: string;\\n        town?: string;\\n        village?: string;\\n        municipality?: string;\\n        suburb?: string;\\n        state_district?: string;\\n        county?: string;\\n        state?: string;\\n        country?: string;\\n      };\\n    };\\n\\n    const addr = data.address;\\n    const cityName =\\n      addr?.city ||\\n      addr?.town ||\\n      addr?.village ||\\n      addr?.municipality ||\\n      addr?.state_district ||\\n      addr?.suburb ||\\n      addr?.county ||\\n      data.name;\\n\\n    if (!cityName) {\\n      return fallback;\\n    }\\n\\n    return {\\n      name: cityName,\\n      admin1: addr?.state,\\n      country: addr?.country || \'Unknown\',\\n      latitude,\\n      longitude,\\n    };\\n  } catch {\\n    return fallback;\\n  }\\n}\", \"StartLine\":240, \"TargetContent\":\"  return (payload.results ?? []).map((item) => ({\\n    name: item.name,\\n    admin1: item.admin1,\\n    country: item.country ?? \'Unknown\',\\n    latitude: item.latitude,\\n    longitude: item.longitude,\\n    timezone: item.timezone,\\n  }));\\n}\", \"TargetFile\":\"/server/openMeteo.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Adding reverse geocoding to Open-Meteo service\", \"toolSummary\":\"Add reverse geocoding helper\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\244|\n\241|\001i\024}\023\v\233\211\034\200Q4\331\214\v\aZG$N!\267D\242\370\267\027?\306\354\331\237\322\321\337\237Q\365\204\2619\344\316\311\360\356\025!F\372\035\375\304-\2274\230\254\223\351\271\346\221\233\207\253\355\235g\223+o\311\t\334j\260\316\367O\260\255\363]h;\325L\303y~\274\vwM&YB\036\022-\v\230Z\251T\000\341\f|h\370f\363zY\334\327t\022\b\317\004\270\303&-\034\t\227V\344\240c\005:pZ\211\030-uX\2739\374\237\217=\327A\351\224yC\256\261\275\362u\r\306\256\242{\032\222\027\246\312.\034)\321|\325\232\277\026D\224\274\r<\337k`\037\234\323](U\355\255\236\300\337h%S\303\034\206\351O\324>\221\216\335\375\252\222\376*\324rb\255\302\266\373\330\230\336\311\332A\236\374\373?\037,\264\a\273\025!\037LoN\r.\247\005\027X\262\340.\312\265\230z\305\230\320\3253\033\242\211w\260\237T\227\221\303\251\025\306+Xh\027\356W\'\367:\342T\300\301\216\245\036\315\371\233\006\246\025XZ\254AK/\346\210L(A\355\376\263\315mj\222$#|I!;^\245\363o-\377[CM\211MYZ\004\230M\204\377%m}\311\371\"\2650\276\037\270\364-\347\030Nr\360\003\235W\244\031\336fP\236\317\025\355\340\233B\2250\367^\177\235\267ennu\242\274\tr\314,\210\272[\r^\234D\252U\354O\v+\311\214\rF\376\205h\376e\027\341\a\t\303\233\266\024,\376|F\005\341\331\aj\232:\r\257I\212\000\344\330Bm\273+\26591K\n\373uvy\234\221\221 \215\341\357\372\t\336\347\224\240\246\\\221\321\240\001\344\r\b\231\253\247\343eJ\241\355\217\263+\177D\003o\352\366\342\226\320E\261\375\277\203\037\201\027*\214\033q\225\372\242\253B\242N\256~i*\264F1Na\n\220\226\024\275\367U\262l\340t\346)1\266\263-{\365\235\246\343r\332\341\235\031+u3\006\017\212Y\277*\316I;\215-.\311\240\017\303\253\345\036\3658\033\016\343\216\327\272y$gA\225`\371r\244\223\2554\366\325$2\360B#\250m\224\213H\311\017\276\305\210LA\233C3\337\315\321\324,\361p\211t\231\260L)\306X\274\3414\247\363)\350\370\256<)`\265\351\363\373\315\334g\016=\'+\267\t\373\264\220]\025q!\212\202\001\023O\022\363\247\340\347\277\000\322,D\244\321\225\213\374l\312M\366\250)A. w\323\