  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Slowdowns Persistently**\n\nI\'m puzzled; even with low thinking levels, `/api/briefing` took an inordinate amount of time. I\'m focusing on why it stalled, especially in relation to `task-105` and its time constraint. I\'m considering switching to `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, but need to finish the tasks first.\n\n\n**Investigating Gemini Latency**\n\nI\'ve got it! I need to compare `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` with `gemini-4-hydrogen`. I was getting slow response times from `gemini-4-hydrogen` with `ThinkingLevel.LOW`, and it turns out `gemini-4-hydrogen` doesn\'t support `ThinkingLevel.MINIMAL`. That means the model *always* thinks before generating, which is causing latency. `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, however, *does* support `ThinkingLevel.MINIMAL`, and should provide JSON more quickly.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Task Completion**\n\nI\'m stopping the immediate model switch for now. Before I change `server/geminiBriefing.ts` to use `\'gemini-3.1-flash-lite\'`, I need to know the output from `task-105`! I\'ll quickly check its status, but since the tool response has to deliver any completed background task system message, I\'ll call `replace_file_content` right away. Also, I\'m shifting focus: I\'ve got to check the **\"on accessing the location kolkata (live location), the data is of New Delhi, fix it\"** issue! I need to account for what `navigator.geolocation` could return and even any caching that could be involved, before even considering a model change.\n\n\n**Debugging Location Inconsistencies**\n\nI\'m seeing inconsistencies with location data and now digging into the \"Use my location\" functionality. I see a New Delhi return from `navigator.geolocation` instead of the expected Kolkata. I\'m investigating potential race conditions and caching issues within `server/openMeteo.ts` and `localStorage`, checking the lat/lon caching key and potentially stale data. I\'m also considering scenarios involving a user with stale location data from before the fix. I\'ll need to figure out how to ensure the current location is reliably reflected, and update the cache key if needed.\n\n\n"
