  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Performance Metrics**\n\nI\'m incredibly pleased with the latest results! The performance difference is remarkable. Before, I was timing out at >20-90 seconds using `gemini-4-hydrogen` at `ThinkingLevel.HIGH`. However, I\'m now down to about 6 seconds cold, and <20ms when cached, using `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` with `ThinkingLevel.MINIMAL`. It\'s a massive improvement!\n\n\n**Optimizing Parallel Processing**\n\nI\'m now focused on achieving near-instantaneous results. The goal is ~2-3 seconds cold for the \"Today\'s Briefing Summary.\" I\'m investigating the initial ~6-second delay, which was largely due to a `curl` sleep. Splitting or parallelizing calls on the server seems key. I\'m considering two lightweight endpoints for parallel execution: one for the initial summary, and another for recommendations, using `Promise.all` to accelerate processing.\n\n\n**Accelerating API Responses**\n\nI\'m incredibly excited about the latest breakthrough! By firing `/api/briefing/summary` and `/api/briefing/actions` concurrently, I\'m achieving significantly faster results. The summary is now displayed in about 1.5-2 seconds, while the actions complete in parallel in ~2.5-3.5 seconds. This drastically reduces the wall-clock latency, and means the \"Today\'s Briefing Summary\" appears almost instantly! I\'m also now reviewing the logic around the live location functionality, to see if there is a bug related to user browser data.\n\n\n**Investigating Location Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the location functionality. I\'ve been tracing the `handleUseGeolocation` function, and I see how user interactions trigger reverse geocoding and subsequent API calls. I\'m focusing on the edge cases: what happens when geolocation fails, or returns unexpected data? How does the app behave when a location is already stored in `localStorage`, and how does this affect subsequent API requests? I\'m exploring the logic in `LocationToolbar.tsx`, especially the `isLocating` state, to ensure a smooth and accurate user experience.\n\n\n**Refining Geolocation Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a critical oversight: the lack of an Enter key handler in the location search input. Previously, if a user typed a city like \"Kolkata\" and pressed Enter, the search would remain on the default location. After inspecting `LocationToolbar.tsx`, I\'ve identified the root cause: an Enter keydown handler was missing! This led to an inconsistent user experience, and I\'m currently implementing a fix to ensure user input is consistently handled.\n\n\n**Implementing User-Friendly Features**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the progress! I\'ve added Enter-key selection to `LocationToolbar.tsx`, so the top search result is immediately selected. I\'ve also added an `useEffect` in `src/App.tsx` to handle the \"Current Location\" issue in `localStorage` by calling `/api/reverse-geocode`. I\'m now implementing the parallel briefing and Enter-key city search!\n\n\n"
    message_id: "KL4Ba5LHHKnbjrEP35C6wQ4"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_8716728884633093926"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import { GoogleGenAI, ThinkingLevel, Type } from \'@google/genai\';\\nimport type {\\n  ActivityGuidanceNote,\\n  AtmosphericSnapshot,\\n  BriefingRecommendation,\\n  DailyBriefing,\\n  HouseholdProfile,\\n} from \'../src/types/air.ts\';\\n\\nexport interface BriefingSummaryPayload {\\n  generatedAt: string;\\n  headlineSummary: string;\\n  inversionExplanation: string;\\n  alert: DailyBriefing[\'alert\'];\\n  activityNotes: ActivityGuidanceNote[];\\n}\\n\\nexport interface BriefingActionsPayload {\\n  generatedAt: string;\\n  recommendations: BriefingRecommendation[];\\n}\\n\\ninterface CacheEntry<T> {\\n  data: T;\\n  expiresAt: number;\\n}\\n\\nconst summaryCache = new Map<string, CacheEntry<BriefingSummaryPayload>>();\\nconst actionsCache = new Map<string, CacheEntry<BriefingActionsPayload>>();\\nconst CACHE_TTL_MS = 5 * 60 * 1000;\\n\\nfunction getAiClient(): GoogleGenAI {\\n  const apiKey = process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY;\\n  if (!apiKey) {\\n    throw new Error(\\n      \'GEMINI_API_KEY is not configured. Please add your Gemini API key in Settings > Secrets.\'\\n    );\\n  }\\n  return new GoogleGenAI({\\n    apiKey,\\n    httpOptions: {\\n      headers: {\\n        \'User-Agent\': \'aistudio-build\',\\n      },\\n    },\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nconst SENSITIVITY_LABELS: Record<HouseholdProfile[\'sensitivity\'], string> = {\\n  general: \'General adult household\',\\n  children: \'Family with young or school-age children\',\\n  seniors: \'Household with older adults (65+)\',\\n  respiratory: \'Household member with asthma or respiratory sensitivity\',\\n};\\n\\nconst COMMUTE_LABELS: Record<HouseholdProfile[\'commute\'], string> = {\\n  car: \'Private car commuter\',\\n  two_wheeler: \'Two-wheeler / scooter commuter\',\\n  transit: \'Public transit / metro / bus commuter\',\\n  walk_cycle: \'Walking or cycling commuter\',\\n};\\n\\nconst HEATING_LABELS: Record<HouseholdProfile[\'heatingCooking\'], string> = {\\n  gas: \'LPG / natural gas cooking & heating\',\\n  electric: \'Electric / induction cooking & heat pump\',\\n  solid_fuel: \'Wood, coal, or biomass nearby/indoors\',\\n};\\n\\nconst INDOOR_LABELS: Record<HouseholdProfile[\'indoorSetup\'], string> = {\\n  hepa_purifier: \'HEPA air purifier at home\',\\n  ac_filter: \'Split AC / HVAC filter without HEPA\',\\n  natural_ventilation: \'Natural window ventilation only\',\\n};\\n\\nfunction makeCacheKey(snapshot: AtmosphericSnapshot, profile: HouseholdProfile): string {\\n  const lat = snapshot.location.latitude.toFixed(2);\\n  const lon = snapshot.location.longitude.toFixed(2);\\n  const aqiBucket = Math.round(snapshot.current.usAqi / 5) * 5;\\n  return `${lat},${lon}|${snapshot.location.name}|${aqiBucket}|${profile.sensitivity}|${profile.commute}|${profile.heatingCooking}|${profile.indoorSetup}|${profile.householdSize}`;\\n}\\n\\nfunction buildContextHeader(snapshot: AtmosphericSnapshot, profile: HouseholdProfile): {\\n  locationLabel: string;\\n  contextText: string;\\n} {\\n  const locationLabel = `${snapshot.location.name}${snapshot.location.admin1 ? `, ${snapshot.location.admin1}` : \'\'}, ${snapshot.location.country}`;\\n  const todayActivities = snapshot.activities\\n    .filter((a) => a.dayIndex === 0)\\n    .map((a) => `${a.id}: ${a.bestWindow} (AQI ${a.windowAvgAqi}, ${a.ratingLabel})`)\\n    .join(\'; \');\\n\\n  const contextText = `City: ${locationLabel} (${snapshot.current.time} ${snapshot.timezone})\\nAir: US AQI ${snapshot.current.usAqi} (${snapshot.current.bandLabel}), Dominant ${snapshot.current.dominantPollutant}, PM2.5 ${snapshot.current.pm25} \302\265g/m\302\263 (${snapshot.current.whoPm25Multiple}x WHO), PM10 ${snapshot.current.pm10}, NO2 ${snapshot.current.no2}, O3 ${snapshot.current.o3}\\nWeather: ${snapshot.current.temperature}\302\260C, RH ${snapshot.current.humidity}%, Wind ${snapshot.current.windSpeed} km/h, Vis ${snapshot.current.visibilityKm} km, Inversion: ${snapshot.inversion.label}\\nVentilation slot: ${snapshot.bestVentilationWindow.windowLabel} (AQI ${snapshot.bestVentilationWindow.avgAqi}, advisable=${snapshot.bestVentilationWindow.advisable})\\nActivity windows: ${todayActivities}\\nHousehold: ${SENSITIVITY_LABELS[profile.sensitivity]}, ${profile.householdSize} people, ${COMMUTE_LABELS[profile.commute]}, ${HEATING_LABELS[profile.heatingCooking]}, ${INDOOR_LABELS[profile.indoorSetup]}.`;\\n\\n  return { locationLabel, contextText };\\n}\\n\\nasync function callWithRetry<T>(fn: () => Promise<T>, maxRetries = 1): Promise<T> {\\n  let lastError: unknown;\\n  for (let attempt = 0; attempt <= maxRetries; attempt++) {\\n    try {\\n      return await fn();\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      lastError = err;\\n      const msg = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err);\\n      const isNonRetryable =\\n        msg.includes(\'API_KEY_INVALID\') ||\\n        msg.includes(\'PERMISSION_DENIED\') ||\\n        msg.includes(\'NOT_FOUND\') ||\\n        msg.includes(\'400\') ||\\n        msg.includes(\'403\') ||\\n        msg.includes(\'404\');\\n      if (isNonRetryable || attempt === maxRetries) {\\n        throw err;\\n      }\\n      await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 350 * (attempt + 1)));\\n    }\\n  }\\n  throw lastError;\\n}\\n\\nexport async function generateBriefingSummary(\\n  snapshot: AtmosphericSnapshot,\\n  profile: HouseholdProfile,\\n  forceRefresh = false\\n): Promise<BriefingSummaryPayload> {\\n  const cacheKey = makeCacheKey(snapshot, profile);\\n  const cached = summaryCache.get(cacheKey);\\n  if (!forceRefresh && cached && cached.expiresAt > Date.now()) {\\n    return cached.data;\\n  }\\n\\n  const ai = getAiClient();\\n  const { locationLabel, contextText } = buildContextHeader(snapshot, profile);\\n\\n  const prompt = `Return concise civic air summary JSON strictly for ${locationLabel}.\\n${contextText}\\n\\nRules (plain English, no emojis, no markdown, concise):\\n- headlineSummary: 2 crisp sentences referencing ${snapshot.location.name}\'s exact AQI/PM2.5 and household priority.\\n- inversionExplanation: 1-2 short sentences on wind, humidity, and dispersion right now.\\n- alert.active: true if US AQI >= 101 or inversion is high, else false. alert.immediateActions: 3 brief actionable phrases.\\n- activityNotes: 1 short sentence each for \\\"school-commute\\\", \\\"outdoor-walk\\\", \\\"cross-ventilation\\\", \\\"children-play\\\", \\\"evening-errands\\\".`;\\n\\n  const response = await callWithRetry(() =>\\n    ai.models.generateContent({\\n      model: \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite\',\\n      contents: prompt,\\n      config: {\\n        thinkingConfig: { thinkingLevel: ThinkingLevel.MINIMAL },\\n        systemInstruction:\\n          \'You are a concise environmental health and urban meteorology advisor. Ground every sentence strictly in the provided city telemetry. Plain English only.\',\\n        responseMimeType: \'application/json\',\\n        responseSchema: {\\n          type: Type.OBJECT,\\n          properties: {\\n            headlineSummary: { type: Type.STRING },\\n            inversionExplanation: { type: Type.STRING },\\n            alert: {\\n              type: Type.OBJECT,\\n              properties: {\\n                active: { type: Type.BOOLEAN },\\n                severityLabel: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                headline: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                immediateActions: {\\n                  type: Type.ARRAY,\\n                  items: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                },\\n              },\\n              required: [\'active\', \'severityLabel\', \'headline\', \'immediateActions\'],\\n            },\\n            activityNotes: {\\n              type: Type.ARRAY,\\n              items: {\\n                type: Type.OBJECT,\\n                properties: {\\n                  activityId: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  tailoredTip: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                },\\n                required: [\'activityId\', \'tailoredTip\'],\\n              },\\n            },\\n          },\\n          required: [\'headlineSummary\', \'inversionExplanation\', \'alert\', \'activityNotes\'],\\n        },\\n      },\\n    })\\n  );\\n\\n  const rawText = (response.text ?? \'\').trim();\\n  if (!rawText) {\\n    throw new Error(\'Gemini returned an empty summary response.\');\\n  }\\n\\n  const parsed = JSON.parse(rawText) as Omit<BriefingSummaryPayload, \'generatedAt\'>;\\n  const result: BriefingSummaryPayload = {\\n    generatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\\n    headlineSummary: parsed.headlineSummary,\\n    inversionExplanation: parsed.inversionExplanation,\\n    alert: {\\n      active: Boolean(parsed.alert?.active),\\n      severityLabel: parsed.alert?.severityLabel || snapshot.current.bandLabel,\\n      headline: parsed.alert?.headline || snapshot.current.advisorySummary,\\n      immediateActions: Array.isArray(parsed.alert?.immediateActions)\\n        ? parsed.alert.immediateActions.slice(0, 3)\\n        : [],\\n    },\\n    activityNotes: Array.isArray(parsed.activityNotes) ? parsed.activityNotes : [],\\n  };\\n\\n  summaryCache.set(cacheKey, { data: result, expiresAt: Date.now() + CACHE_TTL_MS });\\n  return result;\\n}\\n\\nexport async function generateBriefingActions(\\n  snapshot: AtmosphericSnapshot,\\n  profile: HouseholdProfile,\\n  forceRefresh = false\\n): Promise<BriefingActionsPayload> {\\n  const cacheKey = makeCacheKey(snapshot, profile);\\n  const cached = actionsCache.get(cacheKey);\\n  if (!forceRefresh && cached && cached.expiresAt > Date.now()) {\\n    return cached.data;\\n  }\\n\\n  const ai = getAiClient();\\n  const { locationLabel, contextText } = buildContextHeader(snapshot, profile);\\n\\n  const prompt = `Return 6 tailored household air-quality actions in strict JSON for ${locationLabel}.\\n${contextText}\\n\\nRules (plain English, no emojis, no markdown, concise):\\n- Exactly 6 items: 2 with category \\\"routine\\\" (low-emission daily routines), 2 \\\"indoor_hack\\\" (practical indoor air hacks for their indoorSetup & heatingCooking), 2 \\\"sustainable_alternative\\\" (low-emission swaps for their commute/lifestyle).\\n- Keep each text field crisp (1 short sentence). steps: 2 concrete steps per item.\\n- Clearly state directHealthImpact, directEmissionImpact, scientificMechanism, realistic estimatedCo2KgSaved (0.2-8.0), and estimatedExposureDropPct (5-45).\\n- effort must be \\\"Low effort\\\", \\\"Medium effort\\\", or \\\"Habit shift\\\".`;\\n\\n  const response = await callWithRetry(() =>\\n    ai.models.generateContent({\\n      model: \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite\',\\n      contents: prompt,\\n      config: {\\n        thinkingConfig: { thinkingLevel: ThinkingLevel.MINIMAL },\\n        systemInstruction:\\n          \'You are a practical environmental health advisor. Tailor every routine, indoor air hack, and sustainable alternative strictly to the given city air data and household profile. Plain English only.\',\\n        responseMimeType: \'application/json\',\\n        responseSchema: {\\n          type: Type.OBJECT,\\n          properties: {\\n            recommendations: {\\n              type: Type.ARRAY,\\n              items: {\\n                type: Type.OBJECT,\\n                properties: {\\n                  id: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  category: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  title: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  effort: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  timeframe: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  steps: {\\n                    type: Type.ARRAY,\\n                    items: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  },\\n                  directHealthImpact: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  directEmissionImpact: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  scientificMechanism: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  estimatedCo2KgSaved: { type: Type.NUMBER },\\n                  estimatedExposureDropPct: { type: Type.NUMBER },\\n                },\\n                required: [\\n                  \'id\',\\n                  \'category\',\\n                  \'title\',\\n                  \'effort\',\\n                  \'timeframe\',\\n                  \'steps\',\\n                  \'directHealthImpact\',\\n                  \'directEmissionImpact\',\\n                  \'scientificMechanism\',\\n                  \'estimatedCo2KgSaved\',\\n                  \'estimatedExposureDropPct\',\\n                ],\\n              },\\n            },\\n          },\\n          required: [\'recommendations\'],\\n        },\\n      },\\n    })\\n  );\\n\\n  const rawText = (response.text ?? \'\').trim();\\n  if (!rawText) {\\n    throw new Error(\'Gemini returned an empty recommendations response.\');\\n  }\\n\\n  const parsed = JSON.parse(rawText) as { recommendations?: BriefingRecommendation[] };\\n  const validCategories = new Set([\'routine\', \'indoor_hack\', \'sustainable_alternative\']);\\n  const validEfforts = new Set([\'Low effort\', \'Medium effort\', \'Habit shift\']);\\n\\n  const normalizedRecs: BriefingRecommendation[] = (parsed.recommendations ?? []).map(\\n    (rec, idx) => ({\\n      ...rec,\\n      id: rec.id || `rec-${idx + 1}`,\\n      category: (validCategories.has(rec.category)\\n        ? rec.category\\n        : idx < 2\\n          ? \'routine\'\\n          : idx < 4\\n            ? \'indoor_hack\'\\n            : \'sustainable_alternative\') as BriefingRecommendation[\'category\'],\\n      effort: (validEfforts.has(rec.effort)\\n        ? rec.effort\\n        : \'Low effort\') as BriefingRecommendation[\'effort\'],\\n      estimatedCo2KgSaved: Math.max(\\n        0,\\n        Math.round((Number(rec.estimatedCo2KgSaved) || 0.5) * 10) / 10\\n      ),\\n      estimatedExposureDropPct: Math.min(\\n        60,\\n        Math.max(2, Math.round(Number(rec.estimatedExposureDropPct) || 10))\\n      ),\\n      steps: Array.isArray(rec.steps) ? rec.steps.slice(0, 4) : [],\\n    })\\n  );\\n\\n  const result: BriefingActionsPayload = {\\n    generatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\\n    recommendations: normalizedRecs,\\n  };\\n\\n  actionsCache.set(cacheKey, { data: result, expiresAt: Date.now() + CACHE_TTL_MS });\\n  return result;\\n}\\n\\nexport async function generateDailyBriefing(\\n  snapshot: AtmosphericSnapshot,\\n  profile: HouseholdProfile,\\n  forceRefresh = false\\n): Promise<DailyBriefing> {\\n  const [summary, actions] = await Promise.all([\\n    generateBriefingSummary(snapshot, profile, forceRefresh),\\n    generateBriefingActions(snapshot, profile, forceRefresh),\\n  ]);\\n\\n  return {\\n    generatedAt: summary.generatedAt,\\n    headlineSummary: summary.headlineSummary,\\n    inversionExplanation: summary.inversionExplanation,\\n    alert: summary.alert,\\n    activityNotes: summary.activityNotes,\\n    recommendations: actions.recommendations,\\n  };\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Split Gemini generation into parallel low-latency generateBriefingSummary and generateBriefingActions endpoints using gemini-3.1-flash-lite with ThinkingLevel.MINIMAL\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/server/geminiBriefing.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Splitting briefing into fast parallel generators\", \"toolSummary\":\"Split briefing into fast generators\"}"
