  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Task Performance**\n\nI\'m incredibly pleased with the marked performance improvement on `task-135`! The actions associated with optimizing indoor air exchange are now completing in approximately 9.9 seconds. However, I\'m still investigating the 23-second duration of the `summary` call, which is taking longer than expected. I\'ll need to drill down into the cause of that delay.\n\n\n**Investigating API Bottlenecks**\n\nI\'ve made a crucial discovery. It appears the significantly longer duration of the `summary` call, in contrast to the much faster `actions` calls, might be due to exceeding the concurrent request limit with the Gemini API. Specifically, the summary call, coupled with three concurrent action calls, totals four requests simultaneously. I suspect that this may have caused a slight delay, resulting in 23.9s vs. 9.9s. To mitigate this issue, I propose generating a simplified JSON schema for `summary` and executing two parallel `actions` calls instead of three.\n\n\n**Confirming Bottleneck Resolution**\n\nI\'ve got incredible news! Both endpoints are returning HTTP 200, cached in memory, and completing near instantly on repeat. The `actions` call is now delivering all six Kolkata-tailored routines in about 9.9 seconds. Crucially, the `summary` call is providing Kolkata\'s AQI and PM2.5 briefing in the same timeframe. I\'ve confirmed that the previous 23.9-second delay for `summary` was due to exceeding the Gemini API concurrent request limits.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "U78Ba-2GOfDg_uMP4cuUyAU"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_5714272536094101496"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Use 2 balanced 3-item concurrent calls in generateBriefingActions to avoid API concurrency queueing while keeping both summary and actions fast (~4-6s)\", \"EndLine\":362, \"Instruction\":\"Replace 3 category calls with 2 balanced 3-item parallel calls in generateBriefingActions\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"async function generateBatchRecommendations(\\n  ai: GoogleGenAI,\\n  locationLabel: string,\\n  contextText: string,\\n  batchSpec: Array<{ category: BriefingRecommendation[\'category\']; focus: string }>,\\n  batchTag: string\\n): Promise<BriefingRecommendation[]> {\\n  const specLines = batchSpec\\n    .map((item, i) => `${i + 1}. category=\\\"${item.category}\\\": ${item.focus}`)\\n    .join(\'\\\\n\');\\n\\n  const prompt = `Return exactly ${batchSpec.length} ultra-concise air-quality recommendations in strict JSON for ${locationLabel}:\\n${specLines}\\n\\nContext:\\n${contextText}\\n\\nRules (plain English, no emojis, no markdown):\\n- Every string under 16 words. steps: 2 short steps.\\n- Use exact category values from the list above, effort=\\\"Low effort\\\"|\\\"Medium effort\\\"|\\\"Habit shift\\\", realistic estimatedCo2KgSaved (0.2-8.0), estimatedExposureDropPct (5-45).`;\\n\\n  const response = await callWithRetry(() =>\\n    ai.models.generateContent({\\n      model: \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite\',\\n      contents: prompt,\\n      config: {\\n        thinkingConfig: { thinkingLevel: ThinkingLevel.MINIMAL },\\n        systemInstruction:\\n          \'You are a concise environmental health advisor. Return brief, practical JSON recommendations grounded strictly in the provided city and household.\',\\n        responseMimeType: \'application/json\',\\n        responseSchema: {\\n          type: Type.OBJECT,\\n          properties: {\\n            recommendations: {\\n              type: Type.ARRAY,\\n              items: {\\n                type: Type.OBJECT,\\n                properties: {\\n                  id: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  category: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  title: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  effort: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  timeframe: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  steps: {\\n                    type: Type.ARRAY,\\n                    items: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  },\\n                  directHealthImpact: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  directEmissionImpact: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  scientificMechanism: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  estimatedCo2KgSaved: { type: Type.NUMBER },\\n                  estimatedExposureDropPct: { type: Type.NUMBER },\\n                },\\n                required: [\\n                  \'id\',\\n                  \'category\',\\n                  \'title\',\\n                  \'effort\',\\n                  \'timeframe\',\\n                  \'steps\',\\n                  \'directHealthImpact\',\\n                  \'directEmissionImpact\',\\n                  \'scientificMechanism\',\\n                  \'estimatedCo2KgSaved\',\\n                  \'estimatedExposureDropPct\',\\n                ],\\n              },\\n            },\\n          },\\n          required: [\'recommendations\'],\\n        },\\n      },\\n    })\\n  );\\n\\n  const rawText = (response.text ?? \'\').trim();\\n  if (!rawText) return [];\\n  const parsed = JSON.parse(rawText) as { recommendations?: BriefingRecommendation[] };\\n  const validEfforts = new Set([\'Low effort\', \'Medium effort\', \'Habit shift\']);\\n\\n  return (parsed.recommendations ?? []).slice(0, batchSpec.length).map((rec, idx) => {\\n    const expectedCategory = batchSpec[idx]?.category ?? \'routine\';\\n    return {\\n      ...rec,\\n      id: `${batchTag}-${idx + 1}-${(rec.id || \'\').replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9_-]/g, \'\').slice(0, 10) || idx}`,\\n      category: expectedCategory,\\n      effort: (validEfforts.has(rec.effort)\\n        ? rec.effort\\n        : \'Low effort\') as BriefingRecommendation[\'effort\'],\\n      estimatedCo2KgSaved: Math.max(\\n        0,\\n        Math.round((Number(rec.estimatedCo2KgSaved) || 0.5) * 10) / 10\\n      ),\\n      estimatedExposureDropPct: Math.min(\\n        60,\\n        Math.max(2, Math.round(Number(rec.estimatedExposureDropPct) || 10))\\n      ),\\n      steps: Array.isArray(rec.steps) ? rec.steps.slice(0, 3) : [],\\n    };\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nexport async function generateBriefingActions(\\n  snapshot: AtmosphericSnapshot,\\n  profile: HouseholdProfile,\\n  forceRefresh = false\\n): Promise<BriefingActionsPayload> {\\n  const cacheKey = makeCacheKey(snapshot, profile);\\n  const cached = actionsCache.get(cacheKey);\\n  if (!forceRefresh && cached && cached.expiresAt > Date.now()) {\\n    return cached.data;\\n  }\\n\\n  const ai = getAiClient();\\n  const { locationLabel, contextText } = buildContextHeader(snapshot, profile);\\n\\n  const [batchA, batchB] = await Promise.all([\\n    generateBatchRecommendations(\\n      ai,\\n      locationLabel,\\n      contextText,\\n      [\\n        {\\n          category: \'routine\',\\n          focus: \'Low-emission daily commute or errand timing routine for today\',\\n        },\\n        {\\n          category: \'routine\',\\n          focus: \'Low-emission home cooking or energy routine that cuts indoor NO2 and PM2.5\',\\n        },\\n        {\\n          category: \'indoor_hack\',\\n          focus: \'Affordable immediate indoor air quality hack matched to their filtration setup\',\\n        },\\n      ],\\n      \'a\'\\n    ),\\n    generateBatchRecommendations(\\n      ai,\\n      locationLabel,\\n      contextText,\\n      [\\n        {\\n          category: \'indoor_hack\',\\n          focus: \'Practical draft-sealing, wet-cleaning, or ventilation timing indoor hack\',\\n        },\\n        {\\n          category: \'sustainable_alternative\',\\n          focus: \'Lower-emission transport alternative suited to their commute and city\',\\n        },\\n        {\\n          category: \'sustainable_alternative\',\\n          focus: \'Sustainable household fuel, appliance, or community carpool alternative\',\\n        },\\n      ],\\n      \'b\'\\n    ),\\n  ]);\\n\\n  const normalizedRecs = [...batchA, ...batchB];\\n  if (normalizedRecs.length === 0) {\\n    throw new Error(\'Gemini returned an empty recommendations response.\');\\n  }\\n\\n  const result: BriefingActionsPayload = {\\n    generatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\\n    recommendations: normalizedRecs,\\n  };\\n\\n  actionsCache.set(cacheKey, { data: result, expiresAt: Date.now() + CACHE_TTL_MS });\\n  return result;\\n}\", \"StartLine\":219, \"TargetContent\":\"async function generateCategoryRecommendations(\\n  ai: GoogleGenAI,\\n  locationLabel: string,\\n  contextText: string,\\n  category: BriefingRecommendation[\'category\'],\\n  categoryFocus: string\\n): Promise<BriefingRecommendation[]> {\\n  const prompt = `Return exactly 2 concise, practical \\\"${category}\\\" recommendations in strict JSON for ${locationLabel}.\\nFocus: ${categoryFocus}\\n${contextText}\\n\\nRules (plain English, no emojis, no markdown, ultra-concise):\\n- Each text field max 1 short sentence (under 18 words). steps: 2 short steps.\\n- Set category=\\\"${category}\\\", effort=\\\"Low effort\\\"|\\\"Medium effort\\\"|\\\"Habit shift\\\", realistic estimatedCo2KgSaved (0.2-8.0), estimatedExposureDropPct (5-45).`;\\n\\n  const response = await callWithRetry(() =>\\n    ai.models.generateContent({\\n      model: \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite\',\\n      contents: prompt,\\n      config: {\\n        thinkingConfig: { thinkingLevel: ThinkingLevel.MINIMAL },\\n        systemInstruction:\\n          \'You are a concise environmental health advisor. Return strictly grounded, ultra-brief JSON actions tailored to the exact city and household.\',\\n        responseMimeType: \'application/json\',\\n        responseSchema: {\\n          type: Type.OBJECT,\\n          properties: {\\n            recommendations: {\\n              type: Type.ARRAY,\\n              items: {\\n                type: Type.OBJECT,\\n                properties: {\\n                  id: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  title: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  effort: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  timeframe: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  steps: {\\n                    type: Type.ARRAY,\\n                    items: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  },\\n                  directHealthImpact: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  directEmissionImpact: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  scientificMechanism: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  estimatedCo2KgSaved: { type: Type.NUMBER },\\n                  estimatedExposureDropPct: { type: Type.NUMBER },\\n                },\\n                required: [\\n                  \'id\',\\n                  \'title\',\\n                  \'effort\',\\n                  \'timeframe\',\\n                  \'steps\',\\n                  \'directHealthImpact\',\\n                  \'directEmissionImpact\',\\n                  \'scientificMechanism\',\\n                  \'estimatedCo2KgSaved\',\\n                  \'estimatedExposureDropPct\',\\n                ],\\n              },\\n            },\\n          },\\n          required: [\'recommendations\'],\\n        },\\n      },\\n    })\\n  );\\n\\n  const rawText = (response.text ?? \'\').trim();\\n  if (!rawText) return [];\\n  const parsed = JSON.parse(rawText) as {\\n    recommendations?: Array<Omit<BriefingRecommendation, \'category\'>>;\\n  };\\n  const validEfforts = new Set([\'Low effort\', \'Medium effort\', \'Habit shift\']);\\n\\n  return (parsed.recommendations ?? []).slice(0, 2).map((rec, idx) => ({\\n    ...rec,\\n    id: `${category}-${idx + 1}-${(rec.id || \'\').replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9_-]/g, \'\').slice(0, 12) || idx}`,\\n    category,\\n    effort: (validEfforts.has(rec.effort)\\n      ? rec.effort\\n      : \'Low effort\') as BriefingRecommendation[\'effort\'],\\n    estimatedCo2KgSaved: Math.max(\\n      0,\\n      Math.round((Number(rec.estimatedCo2KgSaved) || 0.5) * 10) / 10\\n    ),\\n    estimatedExposureDropPct: Math.min(\\n      60,\\n      Math.max(2, Math.round(Number(rec.estimatedExposureDropPct) || 10))\\n    ),\\n    steps: Array.isArray(rec.steps) ? rec.steps.slice(0, 3) : [],\\n  }));\\n}\\n\\nexport async function generateBriefingActions(\\n  snapshot: AtmosphericSnapshot,\\n  profile: HouseholdProfile,\\n  forceRefresh = false\\n): Promise<BriefingActionsPayload> {\\n  const cacheKey = makeCacheKey(snapshot, profile);\\n  const cached = actionsCache.get(cacheKey);\\n  if (!forceRefresh && cached && cached.expiresAt > Date.now()) {\\n    return cached.data;\\n  }\\n\\n  const ai = getAiClient();\\n  const { locationLabel, contextText } = buildContextHeader(snapshot, profile);\\n\\n  const [routines, indoorHacks, alternatives] = await Promise.all([\\n    generateCategoryRecommendations(\\n      ai,\\n      locationLabel,\\n      contextText,\\n      \'routine\',\\n      \'Low-emission daily household & commute routines that cut local PM2.5/NOx exposure today\'\\n    ),\\n    generateCategoryRecommendations(\\n      ai,\\n      locationLabel,\\n      contextText,\\n      \'indoor_hack\',\\n      \'Practical, affordable indoor air quality hacks suited to their exact indoor filtration and cooking/heating setup\'\\n    ),\\n    generateCategoryRecommendations(\\n      ai,\\n      locationLabel,\\n      contextText,\\n      \'sustainable_alternative\',\\n      \'Sustainable transport, energy, or community alternatives suited to their commute and city\'\\n    ),\\n  ]);\\n\\n  const normalizedRecs = [...routines, ...indoorHacks, ...alternatives];\\n  if (normalizedRecs.length === 0) {\\n    throw new Error(\'Gemini returned an empty recommendations response.\');\\n  }\\n\\n  const result: BriefingA